1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,275
This is a short overview of the new automatic monthly billing for AI Sales Automation.

2
00:00:06,275 --> 00:00:10,160
Tenants can now pay for their plan through UPI AutoPay.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:16,517
They approve once in their UPI app, and Razorpay takes the payment every month after that.

4
00:00:17,617 --> 00:00:21,261
The tenant chooses a plan and presses Subscribe.

5
00:00:21,261 --> 00:00:28,397
They are taken to Razorpay, where they approve a mandate in their UPI app, such as Google Pay.

6
00:00:28,397 --> 00:00:36,368
Once Razorpay confirms the first payment, the plan starts and the plan's credits are added to the wallet.

7
00:00:36,368 --> 00:00:40,771
After that, Razorpay takes each month's payment by itself.

8
00:00:40,771 --> 00:00:42,972
The tenant does nothing more.

9
00:00:44,072 --> 00:00:52,743
On the Billing screen the tenant sees the state of their automatic payment, the monthly amount, and the date of the next payment.

10
00:00:52,743 --> 00:00:59,733
They can cancel whenever they like, after a confirmation, and they keep what they have already paid for.

11
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:06,388
Their payment history shows every attempt, including failed ones with the reason, and each invoice.

12
00:01:07,488 --> 00:01:09,809
Three promises matter most.

13
00:01:09,809 --> 00:01:12,560
First, the price is always ours.

14
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:16,944
It comes from our database, never from the browser.

15
00:01:16,944 --> 00:01:22,274
Second, a plan starts only when Razorpay confirms the payment.

16
00:01:22,274 --> 00:01:26,401
A tenant coming back to our page proves nothing.

17
00:01:26,401 --> 00:01:30,011
Third, credits are added once per payment.

18
00:01:30,011 --> 00:01:36,803
Razorpay sometimes repeats its messages, and a repeat never adds credits twice.

19
00:01:37,903 --> 00:01:42,899
If a payment fails, Razorpay tries again over the next three days.

20
00:01:42,899 --> 00:01:49,106
The plan keeps working through four grace days, and the tenant is told what to do.

21
00:01:49,106 --> 00:01:54,708
If the payment never goes through, the tenant moves back to the free plan.

22
00:01:54,708 --> 00:01:58,038
Credits already in their wallet stay theirs.

23
00:01:58,038 --> 00:02:00,764
A failed payment never adds credits.

24
00:02:01,864 --> 00:02:04,465
The work is built in seven phases.

25
00:02:04,465 --> 00:02:14,260
All two thousand eight hundred and one backend tests pass, and all one thousand five hundred and ninety three screen tests pass.

26
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:18,316
To be clear, those tests use a stand-in for Razorpay.

27
00:02:18,316 --> 00:02:22,065
Nothing has yet been run against Razorpay itself.

28
00:02:23,165 --> 00:02:26,054
Before launch, a few things are needed.

29
00:02:26,054 --> 00:02:30,647
Razorpay must switch on Subscriptions and UPI for our account.

30
00:02:30,647 --> 00:02:40,722
We then run the written test checklist in test mode, and finally one small real mandate, all the way through its second monthly payment.

31
00:02:40,722 --> 00:02:48,649
Two decisions are open: the four grace days, and whether Razorpay's invoice can be used as the tax invoice.

32
00:02:48,649 --> 00:02:54,650
Refunds, credit pack payments and switching between paid plans are not built yet.

33
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:02,908
The feature is off by default, so nothing changes for any tenant until it is switched on.

34
00:03:02,908 --> 00:03:05,803
The next step is the test checklist.

35
00:03:05,803 --> 00:03:06,608
Thank you.

